C. Control Matrix & Lane Algorithm
3-Lane Math: Coordinates at $X \in {-3, 0, 3}$. Smooth lane transitions via Vector3.Lerp / spring physics.
Swipe Left / Right: Single lane switch with responsive banking tilt.
Swipe Up: Jump (obstacle clearance).
Swipe Down: Crouch / Duck under low bridges and branches.
Double Swipe Up: High Jump ($2\times$ height).
Double Swipe Down: Extended ground slide through tight tunnels.
Single Tap Down: Brake / slow down speed ($1\times$).
Double Tap Down: Emergency 2-second pause / hover.
Double Tap Up: Speed Boost ($2\times$).
D. The 3D-5D Dimension Hierarchy
3D (Spatial): WebGL $X, Y, Z$ tracks, obstacles, characters, and particle trails.
4D (Temporal): Dynamic difficulty scaling, daylight/dusk/night cycles, and fluctuating spawn intervals (2–3s, then 5–8s, 6–8s, 3–5s, 11–19s).
5D (Sensory, Cultural & Narrative): Web Audio spatial soundscapes, device haptic vibration feedback (navigator.vibrate), reactive African cultural voice exclamations, and on-chain FIC score multipliers.

