3. Open-Source SDKs & APIs Required
To achieve 100% production-grade execution without reinventing low-level primitives:

1. 3D WebGL Rendering & Game Physics
Three.js (three & @types/three): Already partially present. Used for 3D track meshes, lighting, camera following, and particle systems.
Canvas-Confetti & Shaders: For victory sequences, orb glow effects, and combo visual bursts.
GLTFLoader & DRACOLoader (three/addons): For compressed 3D character skins and urban asset streaming.

2. Audio & Dynamic Voice Lines Engine
Howler.js (howler & @types/howler):
High-performance Web Audio API engine with multi-channel playback, volume fading, and zero-latency audio sprites.
Fixes path bindings to existing assets in /audio/african/ (small-combo.mp3, great-combo.mp3, colossal-combo.mp3, stunning.mp3).
Web Speech API (window.speechSynthesis): Built-in browser speech synthesis with customized African-accented pitch and utterance control for dynamic real-time game commentary.

